        "summary": "Record deposits on a project's Financials page under Contract deposits . Choose Record deposit , then save it as Requested (amount and due date) or Received (amount, date, how it was paid and the check or reference number). If the contract packet sets a deposit percentage, the amount starts from that. Open a requested deposit and choose Record payment when the money arrives. Void removes a deposit you entered by mistake.",
        "content": "Record deposits on a project's **Financials** page under **Contract deposits**. Choose **Record deposit**, then save it as **Requested** (amount and due date) or **Received** (amount, date, how it was paid and the check or reference number). If the contract packet sets a deposit percentage, the amount starts from that. Open a requested deposit and choose **Record payment** when the money arrives. **Void** removes a deposit you entered by mistake.\n\nA received deposit is applied to pay applications before the client pays the balance. By default Compass applies as much of the unapplied deposit as each new draft pay application can take, starting with the oldest draft. On the pay application, **Less deposit applied** shows the amount; type a different amount and choose **Apply amount**, or **Apply automatically** to go back. Admins can turn automatic application off in Settings under **Contract deposits**."
